// Emulator-only rules: everything is allowed.
//
// This file exists so the Firestore emulator has something to load, and is not
// a template for anything a buyer should deploy. The emulator runs against a
// `demo-*` project id, which never touches a real Firebase project and requires
// no credentials, so there is nothing here to secure.
//
// What this deliberately does not do is prove the generated app's security
// rules are correct — the generated app does not produce any. Proving reads and
// writes work is a different claim from proving they are allowed only to the
// right caller, and conflating the two is how an app ships world-readable.
rules_version = '2';

service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if true;
    }
  }
}
